# TPS patch for opensec-pi-subagents — per-agent + aggregate output tok/s
#
# Base:  opensec-git/opensec-pi-subagents master
#        commit 76fd35c4a5e814251badd1f7f523557d3ea7fcf9 (v0.20.9)
# Apply: git apply -p1 <this file>   (from the source root)
#
# What it adds:
#   src/token-rate.ts            rolling 10 s sampler over cumulative OUTPUT
#                                tokens (input/cache are excluded: they step at
#                                API boundaries and spike the rate)
#   src/ui/agent-widget.ts       samples each running agent every frame; shows
#                                `N tok/s` per row and on the `Agents` heading
#   test/token-rate.test.ts      unit tests for the sampler
#   test/agent-widget-tps.test.ts  widget-level per-agent + aggregate rates
#
# Regenerate after editing the working tree:
#   cd <source root> && git add -A && git diff --cached -- src test > 0001-tps.patch
# The updater (scripts/opensec-subagents/update.sh) applies this with --3way;
# a rejected hunk means upstream moved the widget code, so rebase the patch.
#
